id: pm-ikj8ve
title: "Packed Bun SDK import fails on node:module stripTypeScriptTypes"
description: "A real packed Bun 1.3.11 consumer can execute pm through bunx, but importing @unbrained/pm-cli fails before any SDK call because the public SDK bundle statically imports Node-only stripTypeScriptTypes from node:module. Make the eager public SDK import Bun-compatible without weakening Node recovery-producer parsing, and cover the packed Bun path."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:sdk",package-assurance,regression,"runtime:bun"
created_at: "2026-08-17T12:47:48.472Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-17T13:12:17.205Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-17T13:09:03.955Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-17T13:09:03.955Z"
author: "harness:codex"
parent: pm-usfg
resolution: "The recovery analyzer uses a node:module namespace binding and the installed-artifact gate executes listAllComplete under Node and Bun."
expected_result: Importing the packed public SDK works under supported npm/Node and Bun consumers.
actual_result: "Real packed npm/npx and Bun 1.3.11/bunx sessions import the SDK, certify two lifecycle states, and execute package catalog."
